          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Years</strong><br>\nClaude Monet was born on November 14, 1840, in Paris, France. He grew up in Le Havre and began his artistic career by drawing caricatures before transitioning to painting landscapes.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Leader of Impressionism</strong><br>\nMonet became a leader of the Impressionist movement, which sought to capture the transient effects of light and color in nature. His work was characterized by open compositions with an emphasis on the accurate depiction of light in its changing qualities.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Painting \"Impression, Sunrise\"</strong><br>\nThe term \"Impressionism\" is derived from his painting \"Impression, Sunrise.\" This work was displayed in the first of the independent exhibitions of Impressionist art in 1874 and shocked critics with its bold style.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
